{com}. do "W:\Mac_Sync\Desktop\public_release_science_20260904\analytics\Sci_Pat\3_Supplementary_materials\F4_Additional_analyses\03_Sector_heterogeneity\4_section_reg_by_sector.do"
{txt}
{com}. /*******************************************************************************
> Project: Science-linked patents—supplementary sector heterogeneity
> Script:  4_section_reg_by_sector.do
> 
> Purpose:
>   Test whether the sanction effect differs across broad IPC technology sections.
>   Estimate pooled and section-interaction models, then assess robustness by
>   excluding each section in turn for level, log-transformed, and count outcomes.
> 
> Main input (from ${c -(}stata_output{c )-}):
>   - DID_allfirm-level.dta
> 
> Main outputs (under ${c -(}table_output{c )-}):
>   - industry_difference.rtf: pooled and section-interaction estimates
>   - robust_drop_one_industry_1.rtf: leave-one-section-out level estimates
>   - robust_drop_one_industry_2.rtf: leave-one-section-out log estimates
>   - robust_drop_one_industry_3.rtf: leave-one-section-out count estimates
> 
> Notes:
>   The first character of `industry` defines eight broad IPC sections.
> *******************************************************************************/
. 
. * ==============================================================================
. * 1. Construct the broad IPC-section identifier
. * ==============================================================================
. 
. use ${c -(}stata_output{c )-}DID_allfirm-level.dta, clear
{txt}
{com}. 
. bysort industry_id: gen tag1 = (_n == 1) //based on subclass
{txt}
{com}. count if tag1 == 1 //618
  {res}623
{txt}
{com}. 
. gen industry_section = substr(industry, 1, 1)
{txt}
{com}. encode industry_section, gen(industry_section_id)
{txt}
{com}. 
. bysort industry_section_id: gen tag2 = (_n == 1) //based on section
{txt}
{com}. count if tag2 == 1 //8
  {res}8
{txt}
{com}. 
. * ==============================================================================
. * 2. Estimate pooled and section-interaction models
. * ==============================================================================
. 
. * Estimate the level outcome.
. reghdfe f_cite_science_num_w did whether_pat, absorb(firm_id year) vce(r)
{res}{txt}({browse "http://scorreia.com/research/hdfe.pdf":MWFE estimator} converged in 7 iterations)
{res}
{txt}HDFE Linear regression{col 51}Number of obs{col 67}= {res} 2,739,581
{txt}Absorbing 2 HDFE groups{col 51}F({res}   2{txt},{res}2395764{txt}){col 67}= {res}  56492.66
{txt}{col 51}Prob > F{col 67}= {res}    0.0000
{txt}{col 51}R-squared{col 67}= {res}    0.4312
{txt}{col 51}Adj R-squared{col 67}= {res}    0.3495
{txt}{col 51}Within R-sq.{col 67}= {res}    0.0698
{txt}{col 51}Root MSE{col 67}= {res}    0.3474

